nts{/privacy}", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/charliermarsh/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/charliermarsh/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/charliermarsh/gists{/gist_id}", "gravatar_id": "", "html_url": "https://github.com/charliermarsh", "id": 1309177, "login": "charliermarsh", "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjEzMDkxNzc=", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/charliermarsh/orgs", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/charliermarsh/received_events", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/charliermarsh/repos", "site_admin": false, "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/charliermarsh/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/charliermarsh/subscriptions", "type": "User", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/charliermarsh", "user_view_type": "public"}, "comments_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/astral-sh/uv/commits/0397595e532faff5c243c51779e4f28d76da245d/comments", "commit": {"author": {"date": "2025-08-21T15:20:55Z", "email": "charlie.r.marsh@gmail.com", "name": "Charlie Marsh"}, "comment_count": 0, "committer": {"date": "2025-08-21T15:20:55Z", "email": "noreply@github.com", "name": "GitHub"}, "message": "Treat `--upgrade-package` on the command-line as overriding `upgrade = false` in configuration (#15395)\n\n## Summary\n\nRight now, if you put `upgrade = false` in a `uv.toml`, then pass\n`--upgrade-package numpy` on the CLI, we won't upgrade NumPy. This PR\nfixes that interaction by ensuring that when we \"combine\", we look at\nthose arguments holistically (i.e., we bundle `upgrade` and\n`upgrade-package` into a single struct, which then goes through the\n`.combine` logic), rather than combining `upgrade` and `upgrade-package`\nindependently.\n\nIf approved, I then need to add the same thing for `no-build-isolation`,\n`reinstall`, `no-build`, and `no-binary`.", "tree": {"sha": "da806f535df1d617278ae313c926f8fb517a3a36", "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/astral-sh/uv/git/trees/da806f535df1d617278ae313c926f8fb517a3a36"}, "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/astral-sh/uv/git/commits/0397595e532faff5c243c51779e4f28d76da245d", "verification": {"payload": "tree da806f535df1d617278ae313c926f8fb517a3a36\nparent b950453891027f4cd980d3f8c67895c54b4b6750\nauthor Charlie Marsh <charlie.r.marsh@gmail.com> 1755789655 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1755789655 +0100\n\nTreat `--upgrade-package` on the command-line as overriding `upgrade = false` in configuration (#15395)\n\n## Summary\n\nRight now, if you put `upgrade = false` in a `uv.toml`, then pass\n`--upgrade-package numpy` on the CLI, we won't upgrade NumPy. This PR\nfixes that interaction by ensuring that when we \"combine\", we look at\nthose arguments holistically (i.e., we bundle `upgrade` and\n`upgrade-package` into a single struct, which then goes through the\n`.combine` logic), rather than combining `upgrade` and `upgrade-package`\nindependently.\n\nIf approved, I then need to add the same thing for `no-build-isolation`,\n`reinstall`, `no-build`, and `no-binary`.", "reason": "valid", "signature": "-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJopzlXCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAoAEQAGJE0mnozMRIcClFM0rQK9MF\nA+wRS+BDHV/tJZb/SCM0A3n1XdruEBywE2VqyyC/VSrduiGqypsF2KLXYVtExqcL\nmjwlRN9KW+/VHeXhte2a8ymlTmNzJYEQRcruSF4eH/nh2QEyE1Tqz6GyZ2DcVaPR\nV3x+DUjysm3l9Rlgo8/2e1EmDE0qRb4nmvG5SYhXV8vYZUpmqp9mqbhgV+cF75dZ\nYN9zZIW8unBCHFDdXQ38PW2qClBiaK6oE0KcCVTYob+dsVjpFZ5/GKwqctoeM3ej\nrzal1yBz+HriLFdIu6preAVnbMAas2FrUTcDbvN7rIgP10Z7xsm7F1nIfztwS3K1\nyc1Go+KrtXAfl4oKucn+eQ/at5xCGhT1QgIXdbqjroV9xuve7CFOWyXkHP9nVbDN\nDpWvL2ocpFvxyfkhtl6FtSFrAfNA0EjssiX27oh+zl+Kd1toBhybs0thDh4GnU/u\n31r5euBkaLbg4DHAQNZ0TtpsHO4p8/Zpo4yBVAgGp8gVk4mECX8AZt63B6r/CE9n\nNjLIuy//tSQx+uTLpO/kxBbkx5qpcDm8w/qb1kdAG8K04xKkc+uiIC+dVg1Phs4y\nGVhTasDkqo/1HEzy6kzyfFz6WL/0H6MDiP7vWF28+QXjYGvz1zzodtKy/ZTnIiwK\n23B115jPv5kkfgypC/XD\n=U0NZ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n", "verified": true, "v